IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `clatas-dates`

-- Civil Liability Act 2002 (Tas) -- what every Part needs: the claims s 3B takes out of the Act, and the dates s 4 sets
-- for each Part. Asked from the seat of the person bringing the claim.
--
-- s 3B(1): "This Act does not apply to or in respect of civil liability -- (a) in respect of an intentional act that is
-- done with intent to cause injury or death or that is sexual assault or other sexual misconduct; or (b) relating to an
-- award of damages for personal injury or death where the injury or death concerned resulted from smoking or other use
-- of tobacco products." (1A): "Despite subsection (1), Parts 4 and 10C apply in respect of an intentional act that is
-- child abuse, within the meaning of section 49J(3)." (2): "This Act, except Parts 2, 3, 5 and 5A, Divisions 1, 2, 3, 4
-- and 7 of Part 6 and Parts 7 and 8, does not apply to or in respect of civil liability relating to an injury to which
-- Part III of the Motor Accidents (Liabilities and Compensation) Act 1973 applies." (3): not to "an injury to which
-- Division 2 of Part X of the Workers Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988 applies". (4): not to "liability for
-- compensation under the Workers Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988, the Asbestos-Related Diseases (Occupational
-- Exposure) Compensation Act 2011, the Criminal Injuries Compensation Act 1976 or the Anti-Discrimination Act 1998 or a
-- scheduled benefit under the Motor Accidents (Liabilities and Compensation) Act 1973". (5): regulations may exclude
-- further classes; none is deposited (NOTES.md).
--
-- s 4 dates. Parts 2, 3 and 4: not "a cause of action accrued before the commencement of this Act" (s 4(1)); the Act
-- commences "on a day to be proclaimed" (s 2) and the day is not in the deposited text, so it is asked as a fact. Part 5
-- and s 12: any accrual (s 4(2)). Part 6 other than s 12, and Parts 7, 8, 9, 10 and 11: not accrued "before 4 July
-- 2003" (s 4(3)). ss 28A to 28D: not before the commencement of the Civil Liability Amendment Act 2005 (s 4(3A)), and
-- s 28BA: not before s 9 of the Civil Liability Amendment Act 2013 (s 4(3B)); Part 9A: not before the Civil Liability
-- Amendment (Proportionate Liability) Act 2005 (s 4(4)); Parts 8A and 8B: not before the Civil Liability Amendment Act
-- 2008 (s 4(5)); Part 10B: only "a cause of action accrued after the commencement of that Part" (s 4(6)). Those
-- commencement days are read from the editorial history notes on the inserted sections ("Applied:15 Dec 2005",
-- "Applied:01 Mar 2014", "Applied:01 Jun 2005", "Applied:22 Oct 2008", "Applied:30 May 2012"); fork F1 in NOTES.md.
--
-- Copyright (c) State of Tasmania. Quoted from an unofficial plain-text copy under CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- Based on material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at 6 November 2026.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `What the Act reaches (ss 3B, 4)`

-- The kind of claim, for s 3B. A claim in more than one class: choose the first that fits.
DECLARE `The kind of claim` IS ONE OF
    `an ordinary claim: none of the s 3B exclusions`
    `an intentional act that is child abuse within s 49J(3) (s 3B(1A))`
    `another intentional act done with intent to cause injury or death, or sexual assault or other sexual misconduct (s 3B(1)(a))`
    `personal injury or death that resulted from smoking or other use of tobacco products (s 3B(1)(b))`
    `an injury Part III of the Motor Accidents (Liabilities and Compensation) Act 1973 applies to (s 3B(2))`
    `an injury Division 2 of Part X of the Workers Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988 applies to (s 3B(3))`
    `compensation under the workers compensation, asbestos diseases, criminal injuries or anti-discrimination Acts, or a motor accidents scheduled benefit (s 3B(4))`

-- The Parts, and the sections that carry their own start dates.
DECLARE `The provision` IS ONE OF
    `Part 2 (intoxication)`
    `Part 3 (recovery by criminals)`
    `Part 4 (apologies)`
    `Part 5 (structured settlements)`
    `Part 5A (provisional damages)`
    `Part 6 Divisions 1 to 4 and 7 (breach of duty, causation, obvious risks, contributory negligence)`
    `Part 6 Divisions 5 and 6 (dangerous recreational activities, professional negligence)`
    `Part 7 (assessment of damages), other than ss 28A to 28D and 28BA`
    `ss 28A to 28D (discount rate, gratuitous services, motor accidents, consortium)`
    `s 28BA (loss of capacity to provide gratuitous services)`
    `Part 8 (mental harm)`
    `Part 8A (good samaritans)`
    `Part 8B (food donors)`
    `Part 9 (public and other authorities)`
    `Part 9A (proportionate liability)`
    `Part 10 (volunteers)`
    `Part 10A (accommodation providers)`
    `Part 10B (employer and employee)`
    `Part 10C (child abuse, liability of organisations)`

-- s 3B(2) keeps these for a motor accidents Part III injury.
GIVEN p IS A `The provision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `kept for a motor accidents injury (s 3B(2))` p IF
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `Part 2 (intoxication)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Part 3 (recovery by criminals)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Part 5 (structured settlements)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Part 5A (provisional damages)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Part 6 Divisions 1 to 4 and 7 (breach of duty, causation, obvious risks, contributory negligence)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Part 7 (assessment of damages), other than ss 28A to 28D and 28BA` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `ss 28A to 28D (discount rate, gratuitous services, motor accidents, consortium)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 28BA (loss of capacity to provide gratuitous services)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Part 8 (mental harm)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN p IS A `The provision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `kept for child abuse (s 3B(1A))` p IF
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `Part 4 (apologies)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Part 10C (child abuse, liability of organisations)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN p IS A `The provision`, k IS A `The kind of claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3B leaves the provision to apply` p k IF
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `an ordinary claim: none of the s 3B exclusions` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an intentional act that is child abuse within s 49J(3) (s 3B(1A))` THEN `kept for child abuse (s 3B(1A))` p
    WHEN `an injury Part III of the Motor Accidents (Liabilities and Compensation) Act 1973 applies to (s 3B(2))` THEN `kept for a motor accidents injury (s 3B(2))` p
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- The commencement days used by s 4, from the history notes (fork F1).
`4 July 2003 (s 4(3))` MEANS `the calendar date` 4 7 2003
`the Civil Liability Amendment Act 2005 commenced` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 12 2005
`s 9 of the Civil Liability Amendment Act 2013 commenced` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 3 2014
`the Proportionate Liability Act 2005 commenced` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 6 2005
`the Civil Liability Amendment Act 2008 commenced` MEANS `the calendar date` 22 10 2008
`Part 10B commenced` MEANS `the calendar date` 30 5 2012
`Part 10C commenced` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 5 2020

-- "not ... accrued before" a day: a cause of action accrued on that day is reached.
GIVEN `the accrual` IS A DATE, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `not before` `the accrual` `the start` IF NOT (`the accrual` `falls before` `the start`)

GIVEN p IS A `The provision`, `the accrual` IS A DATE, `accrued before the Act commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4 reaches a cause of action accrued then` p `the accrual` `accrued before the Act commenced` IF
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `Part 2 (intoxication)` THEN (NOT `accrued before the Act commenced`)
    WHEN `Part 3 (recovery by criminals)` THEN (NOT `accrued before the Act commenced`)
    WHEN `Part 4 (apologies)` THEN (NOT `accrued before the Act commenced`)
    WHEN `Part 5 (structured settlements)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Part 5A (provisional damages)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `ss 28A to 28D (discount rate, gratuitous services, motor accidents, consortium)` THEN `not before` `the accrual` `the Civil Liability Amendment Act 2005 commenced`
    WHEN `s 28BA (loss of capacity to provide gratuitous services)` THEN `not before` `the accrual` `s 9 of the Civil Liability Amendment Act 2013 commenced`
    WHEN `Part 8A (good samaritans)` THEN `not before` `the accrual` `the Civil Liability Amendment Act 2008 commenced`
    WHEN `Part 8B (food donors)` THEN `not before` `the accrual` `the Civil Liability Amendment Act 2008 commenced`
    WHEN `Part 9A (proportionate liability)` THEN `not before` `the accrual` `the Proportionate Liability Act 2005 commenced`
    WHEN `Part 10A (accommodation providers)` THEN TRUE
    -- "accrued after the commencement": accrual on the day of commencement is read as after it (fork F2).
    WHEN `Part 10B (employer and employee)` THEN `not before` `the accrual` `Part 10B commenced`
    -- Part 10C: ss 49H and 49J carry their own dates (s 4(7), (8)), Division 4 reaches any abuse (s 4(9)).
    WHEN `Part 10C (child abuse, liability of organisations)` THEN TRUE
    -- Part 6 (other than s 12), Parts 7, 8, 9, 10: s 4(3).
    OTHERWISE `not before` `the accrual` `4 July 2003 (s 4(3))`

GIVEN p IS A `The provision`, k IS A `The kind of claim`, `the accrual` IS A DATE, `accrued before the Act commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provision applies to my claim` p k `the accrual` `accrued before the Act commenced` IF
        `s 3B leaves the provision to apply` p k
    AND `s 4 reaches a cause of action accrued then` p `the accrual` `accrued before the Act commenced`

@export Does this Part of the Civil Liability Act 2002 (Tas) apply to my claim (ss 3B, 4)? The Act does not apply to intentional harm, sexual assault, tobacco, workers compensation and some other claims, keeps only some Parts for motor accident injuries, and each Part reaches only causes of action that accrued after its start date.
GIVEN p IS A `The provision` @desc The Part of the Act you are asking about.
      k IS A `The kind of claim` @desc What kind of claim yours is. If more than one fits, the first that fits.
      `the day my cause of action accrued` IS A DATE @desc The day your cause of action accrued (usually the day you were harmed). ISO date.
      `it accrued before the Act commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your cause of action accrue before the Civil Liability Act 2002 commenced (a day proclaimed under s 2)? Only Parts 2, 3 and 4 use this.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Does this Part of the Act apply to my claim` p k `the day my cause of action accrued` `it accrued before the Act commenced` MEANS
    `the provision applies to my claim` p k `the day my cause of action accrued` `it accrued before the Act commenced`
